PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported)
  clamp / ±8 / Home 80 / End max      → DataTableResizeMath (pure, Sendable, off-actor); round = half-away
                                        -from-zero (== JS Math.round on the positive width domain).
  pointer down/move/up                → DragGesture(minimumDistance:0): begin captures start width, change
                                        fires onResize(clamp(startWidth+translation)), end fires onResizeEnd.
  ArrowLeft/Right/Home/End            → .onKeyPress(.leftArrow/.rightArrow/.home/.end) (iOS 17+/macOS 14+).
  role=separator + aria-valuenow      → SwiftUI accessibility adjustable: .accessibilityLabel/.Value/.Hint +
                                        .accessibilityAdjustableAction (VoiceOver one-finger swipe = ±8).
  aria-label "Resize column {key}"    → DataTableResizerStrings.label(columnKey:override:) (P1/S10), label
                                        override honoured exactly like the web `label ??`.
  dragging opacity-100 bg-cyan-400/60 → DataTableResizerStyle(.dragging): full opacity + accent tint
                                        (Color.TS.accent); idle = faint neutral hairline (always-on touch
                                        affordance), hover/focus reveal, focus adds the platform ring.
  cursor: col-resize                  → NSCursor.resizeLeftRight on hover (#if os(macOS)).
  onClick stopPropagation (no sort)   → the sort Button and the resize handle are separate hit targets in
                                        DataTableResizableHeaderCell; dragging the handle never sorts.
  i18n  : zero English literals in code; the one web string + native a11y/showcase prose live in P1/S10.
  a11y  : label + value + hint on the handle; adjustable action only when resizable; non-resizable column is
          inert + non-focusable (native peer of the Windows CanResize guard). RTL + Dynamic-Type-XXL previews.
  telemetry : view.opened surface="DataTableResizer" via reportOpenIfNeeded (P1/S11), default OSLog sink.

